## Founding & History
Uplands Vineyard is situated on a historic property in Tasmania's Coal River Valley, with roots dating back to 1823. The original house on the property was built around 1823 by John Petchey, a former convict who became an entrepreneur. The land was later purchased by William Farquhar McKay on May 15, 1848, when it comprised 1,560 acres. Over two centuries, only four families have owned this land. Viticulture in the Coal River Valley began in 1973, and Chardonnay vines were first planted at Uplands in 1998. The vineyard opened its cellar door for the Southern Open Vineyards Weekend in 2020.

## People
Uplands Vineyard is owned and operated by Michael and Debbie. They are described as hands-on custodians, closely involved in every stage of the winemaking process, from vine to bottle. Michael and Debbie purchased the property in 1997.

## Vineyard & Site
Uplands Vineyard is a small, family-run vineyard in the Coal River Valley. The property spans four hectares, with half a hectare planted to Chardonnay vines and another half hectare recently added for Pinot Noir. The grapes benefit from the unique climate of the Coal River Valley, which provides significant rainfall in winter and spring, followed by long, sunny days in late summer and early autumn. This balance allows for slow ripening, developing flavor ripeness and natural acidity in the grapes. Chardonnay vines were first planted in 1998.

## Cellar Door Experience
Uplands Vineyard has a new cellar door that operates by appointment only. This allows for a more personal and unhurried tasting experience. Visitors can expect relaxed and informative tastings, guided by the owners, where they can learn about the vineyard's history, winemaking approach, and the stories behind each wine. The historic cellar door is located in a sandstone building with a deck overlooking gardens and out to the water. Private wine tastings are available for intimate gatherings or special occasions. Buses and coaches are accepted by appointment only.

## Food & Hospitality
Uplands Vineyard occasionally hosts intimate events. They are also open to hosting private functions, such as milestone birthdays, hen's celebrations, corporate gatherings, or Christmas parties. For private functions, they can tailor the experience, including options for BYO food or liaising with caterers or food vans. Uplands Vineyard hosted a "Dark Shed - A winter feast of fire, wine and flavour" event, featuring a five-course menu crafted by chef Paul Willcock and Sara, with thoughtfully paired wines in an intimate setting with open flames and lanterns. PW Catering has also provided smoked meats with seasonal salads for events.

## Awards & Recognition
Uplands Vineyard produces award-winning Sparkling and Chardonnay. They have received a trophy for their Blanc de Blancs at the Royal Hobart Wine Show 2025.

## Sustainability & Certifications
No reliable information found from public sources.

## Visiting Practical Info
The address for Uplands Vineyard is 174 Richmond Rd, Cambridge, Hobart, Tasmania, 7170. The phone number is 0409 413 684. Their website is uplandsvineyard.com.au. The vineyard is open for tastings by appointment. The property has disabled access available; visitors are advised to contact the operator for details.

## Notable / Distinctive
Uplands Vineyard is distinguished by its deep connection to Tasmania's early colonial history, with the property dating back to 1823. The house on the property was built by John Petchey, a former convict. The vineyard emphasizes craftsmanship, small-scale production, and personal hospitality. It is a family-run vineyard. The historic cellar door is in a sandstone building with a deck overlooking gardens and water.

